title: intro
---
You find yourself at The Meeting House.

You are Mother. 

As the doors close behind you, a gust of summer air blows into the space. Your hair is plastered to your forehead and neck.

The whispers, cries, and prayers of the attending townspeople are nearly as suffocating as their body odor.
-> It's simple and austere. It serves its purpose well.
-> It's stuffy and distracting. Not an ounce of room to breathe.
-> It's heavy and intense. You've witnessed girls meet their final fate here.

Narrow wooden benches, occupied by village men, are shoved up against the rough-hewn walls. Candlelight casts an orange shimmer across the dark canopy overhead. But that matters not to you.

There's one person, and only one person, on your mind.

Your daughter, Prudence. The Maiden.

You look frantically around for her...but she is nowhere in sight.
<<jump observing>>
